  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating the impact of drought for the most vulnerable pastoral and agropastoral communities of Turkana and Wajir Counties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this project is to safeguard livestock-based livelihoods and improve the lives, food security, and nutrition status of drought-affected households.
This FAO project provides cash plus livestock Feed, Animal health services, and collapsible water tanks in support of livestock water trucking to target pastoralists in dry-season grazing areas.
In total, the project is targeting 42,399 people, including 10,117 women and 25,498 children. 1,696 persons with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
